cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use or adapt this lab, please cite it as below."
title: "The Pain–Comfort Lab: Looking Inside a Language Model"
abstract: >-
  A curiosity-driven, inquiry-based lab for beginners with basic machine-learning
  knowledge but no transformer experience. Across eight Jupyter notebooks, students
  take snapshots of an open language model's internal activations, find a
  pain-to-comfort direction, test it against a sealed test set and controls
  (shuffled labels, random directions, a bag-of-words baseline), nudge the model
  along it (activation steering), and design their own investigation. Every step
  includes code walk-throughs that show what each line returns, why each data
  structure and parameter was chosen, and how to inspect shapes.
type: software
